{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795378316,"nonce":"1UQRzFlA2c7EyZCvU/8FO77fS+o=","message":"Cross builds hit the same decision. ash --build --target x86_64-apple-darwin --native-lib libgreeter.a main.hl, run on an arm64 Mac, fails with: Required library 'greeter' not found in the output directory. The target is a desktop triple, so native_dynamic_loading is true and the build looks for greeter.hdll to load; there is no x86_64 .hdll, only the x86_64 staticlib. Deciding static natives per build covers it: when the archives define every non-runtime native, the archive::defined_symbols filter removes them from the set that must be found as HDLLs, and the build links the static runtime for the triple. Needs an ash_std built for the triple, as the mobile cross builds do. Reproducer from the hxn session: hxn package hl --target x86_64-apple-darwin in ~/Vibranium/hxn/examples/greeter, then hxn package hl app.hxml --target x86_64-apple-darwin --ash \u003cash\u003e.","files":null}]}